It's time to play.

259
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:40,006
Now, who should I kill first?

260
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:47,030
See ya?

261
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:52,037
He had his pick of the deadliest
criminals in the world,

262
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:53,597
and he had them fight to the death!

263
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:55,637
while he simply stood there and watched?

264
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:58,485
Yes, but only four of
the prisoners were taken.

265
00:15:58,700 --> 00:16:03,680
San Juan Wolf, Avalo Pizarro, Vasco
Schott, and Katarina Devon, as you saw.

266
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,560
But I'm sorry to say, sir,

267
00:16:05,980 --> 00:16:10,397
that his new recruits aren't the only
prisoners who are missing from Level 6.

268
00:16:10,480 --> 00:16:11,310
I...

269
00:16:19,160 --> 00:16:24,800
So Impel Down is swimming with escaped
criminals, the worst the world has ever seen.

270
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:27,617
We can't let a single
one of them get away.

271
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:30,777
If they stole a ship and slipped
into some country unnoticed,

272
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:33,717
there's no telling what sort of
terrible things might happen.

273
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:37,057
Start a count of how many
level 6 prisoners are missing?

274
00:16:37,140 --> 00:16:41,375
You have their names and put out a
most wanted list as soon as possible.

275
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:43,900
What's wrong?

276
00:16:44,760 --> 00:16:46,280
Well, uh, actually.

277
00:16:47,660 --> 00:16:50,157
I'm under direct orders
from the world government

278
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:52,797
to keep this matter a secret at any cost!.

279
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:58,020
A huge blunder like this one could
badly hurt the government's reputation?.

280
00:17:02,800 --> 00:17:04,480
I don't give a damn!

281
00:17:34,180 --> 00:17:35,740
Doflamingo, you bastard!

282
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:40,000
Come on, lighten up.

283
00:17:40,140 --> 00:17:42,637
We both know you're too
weak to be a warlord.

284
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:43,700
Just face it.

285
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:47,100
I'll do you a favor for old time's sake.

286
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:49,477
We won't say the government
had you put down.

287
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:51,854
We'll say you gave your life in battle.

288
00:17:52,460 --> 00:17:54,620
So Sengoku put you up to this.

289
00:17:54,820 --> 00:17:56,780
I'll tear him apart. Nah.

290
00:17:58,120 --> 00:18:00,040
Think higher up the ladder.

291
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,977
A pirate ship is approaching
Laskop in the West Blue,

292
00:18:25,060 --> 00:18:27,417
but we don't have any
forces nearby that can help.

293
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:29,200
Contact the closest base.

294
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:33,635
Reinforcements from the 80th
Division are on their way.

295
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,353
This is the South Blue.

296
00:18:36,620 --> 00:18:38,577
Currently checking the
location of the attack.

297
00:18:38,660 --> 00:18:39,490
Damn it!

298
00:18:39,573 --> 00:18:41,537
The pirates are supposed
to be afraid of us.

299
00:18:41,620 --> 00:18:43,837
Headquarters dealt them a
major blow at Marineford.

300
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:46,237
Not to mention Whitebeard
is dead, so what gives?

301
00:18:46,320 --> 00:18:48,497
You would have thought they'd
be laying low after the war,

302
00:18:48,580 --> 00:18:50,097
but they're running wild everywhere.

303
00:18:50,180 --> 00:18:52,474
I wonder what's gotten into those guys.

304
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:54,835
Pirates have started raiding Lost Cop.

305
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:56,777
Communication has also been lost.

306
00:18:56,860 --> 00:18:58,213
Proceed to send backup.

307
00:18:58,480 --> 00:19:00,520
I repeat, send backup now.

308
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:04,260
All right, boys, load her up.

309
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:06,915
After that, it's on to the Grand Line!

310
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:08,030
Yeah!

311
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:14,777
Two weeks after the War
of the Best concluded,

312
00:19:14,860 --> 00:19:18,801
the world began to witness the
consequences of Whitebeard's defeat.

313
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:23,630
No!

314
00:19:23,713 --> 00:19:25,237
You guys aren't welcome here!

315
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:27,220
Get out of our town!

316
00:19:30,980 --> 00:19:32,860
You didn't hear the news?

317
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:42,689
Then let me tell you, this dump's been
up for grabs since Whitebeard croaked.

318
00:19:42,780 --> 00:19:45,133
This stupid flag don't mean a thing now.

319
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:47,080
That's right.

320
00:19:47,340 --> 00:19:49,340
There's no one to protect you now!

321
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:11,040
Hey, Twerp, listen up, because
I'm only going to say this once.

322
00:20:11,360 --> 00:20:13,560
This island's under my control now.

323
00:20:13,860 --> 00:20:16,980
The name's Brownbeard,
and don't you forget it.

324
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:24,397
The war ended with the death of
Whitebeard and a Navy victory.

325
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:28,277
Yet the peace that the world
government hoped to achieve slipped

326
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:32,595
through their fingers and the world
was only plunged into further unrest

327
00:20:34,460 --> 00:20:36,560
Meanwhile, aboard the Kuja ship,

328
00:20:36,980 --> 00:20:38,274
Boa Hancock, Gene Bay,

329
00:20:38,460 --> 00:20:40,837
and the Heart Pirates make
their way toward Amazon

330
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:44,580
Lily Where they will shelter
the unconscious Luffy

331
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:48,860
Now then,

332
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:54,960
this chapter of Straw Boys Live co-starring
yours truly has come to a close Hee-haw!

333
00:20:55,580 --> 00:20:59,317
Jinbei, I hope you don't mind
watching over our friend in my place.

334
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:02,160
Of course, my body is
still too weak to swim,

335
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:06,242
but the least that I can do is
watch over Luffy until he recovers.

336
00:21:07,020 --> 00:21:10,760
Though, I fear there is precious
little aid I can give him.

337
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:15,400
It was a curious twist of fate
to meet you, Fishman. Likewise.

338
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:19,077
Although we were both imprisoned
in the lowest levels of Impel Down,

339
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:20,925
our paths nearly didn't cross.

340
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:23,860
Luffy carried us away like a tidal wave,

341
00:21:24,060 --> 00:21:27,942
though I must admit I know not the
direction that these seas flow.

342
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:30,280
Tidal wave is right.

343
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:34,220
His antics at Marineford were
too turbulent even for us.

344
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:37,680
I hate to say goodbye, my friend,

345
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:40,057
but the candy boys and girls of my kingdom

346
00:21:40,140 --> 00:21:42,740
can only wait on their master for so long.

347
00:21:43,140 --> 00:21:45,200
Do take care of Strawboy for me!

348
00:21:45,380 --> 00:21:46,600
I shall miss him!

349
00:21:51,060 --> 00:21:52,620
So long, bye!

350
00:21:53,080 --> 00:21:54,737
Thanks for everything, Straw Hat!

351
00:21:54,820 --> 00:21:58,457
We'll tell tales of you in
Kamabaka Kingdom for years to come!

352
00:21:58,540 --> 00:22:00,977
When he wakes up, be
sure to say hi for us!

353
00:22:01,060 --> 00:22:02,740
Get real soon, Straw Boy!

354
00:22:02,880 --> 00:22:04,577
We can't wait to see you again!

355
00:22:04,660 --> 00:22:05,542
Right in there!

356
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:07,520
Everything's gonna be okay!

357
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:11,300
Let's go, my darlings! Yeah!

358
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:13,286
Off to the newcomer paradise!

359
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:16,220
Keep leading the way, Queen Eva! Yes, sir!

360
00:22:16,600 --> 00:22:18,580
Peachy Island, here we come!

361
00:22:19,340 --> 00:22:23,222
I hate to ruin the moment, but we
really should be on our way now.

362
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,440
Two weeks have passed.

363
00:22:27,120 --> 00:22:29,680
Law and his crew are staying in the bay,

364
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:34,136
continuing to treat Luffy's injuries
without encroaching on the island.

365
00:22:46,760 --> 00:22:50,357
Someone grab him he's
lost his mind what will

366
00:22:50,440 --> 00:22:52,911
happen to him if he remains in that state?

367
00:22:53,600 --> 00:22:56,877
Simple if he keeps
flailing around the more

368
00:22:56,960 --> 00:22:59,757
likely he is to open his
wound and if that happens!

369
00:22:59,840 --> 00:23:01,460
Chances are he'll die.

370
00:23:05,320 --> 00:23:06,500
That was our chance!

371
00:23:07,100 --> 00:23:08,820
Dammit, get off me!

372
00:23:09,140 --> 00:23:12,220
Just hold still! Shut up! Let me go!

373
00:23:14,660 --> 00:23:16,940
Where did they take you?

374
00:23:17,360 --> 00:23:18,920
Where did you go?

375
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:21,520
He's gone completely mad.

376
00:23:22,140 --> 00:23:22,970
Oh, Luffy.

377
00:23:23,140 --> 00:23:25,316
We've got to tell the snake princess.

378
00:23:25,940 --> 00:23:26,770
Princess!

379
00:23:27,060 --> 00:23:29,020
We have big news! Are you there?

380
00:23:30,620 --> 00:23:32,420
Luffy is finally woken up.

381
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:34,520
Luffy is awake! Are you sure?

382
00:23:34,820 --> 00:23:35,937
Oh, thank goodness.

383
00:23:36,020 --> 00:23:39,020
I must rush to his side
immediately. You cannot!

384
00:23:40,060 --> 00:23:42,840
The kingdom is obsessed
with seeing those men.

385
00:23:43,140 --> 00:23:47,897
How can you expect them to follow our laws
if you so readily break them yourself?

386
00:23:47,980 --> 00:23:50,400
Men are prohibited in our land.

387
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:55,780
Luffy is one thing, but I cringe at how
easily we let these strangers into the bay.

388
00:23:56,300 --> 00:23:58,380
Must you keep bending the rules?

389
00:23:59,100 --> 00:24:00,837
Yes, I know, but he needs help.

390
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:03,437
Before worrying about that,
you should eat something.

391
00:24:03,520 --> 00:24:04,696
Your sister's right.

392
00:24:04,820 --> 00:24:08,840
Since you returned to Amazon Lily,
you've barely eaten a bite. Food?

393
00:24:09,040 --> 00:24:11,577
Yes, Luffy must be starving
after his recovery.

394
00:24:11,660 --> 00:24:12,597
He will need his strength.

395
00:24:12,680 --> 00:24:15,317
Go prepare a mountain of
dishes rich in nutrients.

396
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:16,760
Yes, as you wish.

397
00:24:16,960 --> 00:24:18,548
And I shall aid you myself.

398
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:20,802
Onward to the kitchen for Luffy.

399
00:24:21,280 --> 00:24:22,927
Whatever you want, princess.

400
00:24:23,080 --> 00:24:24,977
I can let this one pass.

401
00:24:25,060 --> 00:24:26,857
So she wants to do some cooking.

402
00:24:26,940 --> 00:24:28,400
You harm in that.

403
00:24:28,580 --> 00:24:31,120
When we're done, I'll serve him myself.

404
00:24:31,440 --> 00:24:32,793
Are you even listening?

405
00:24:33,200 --> 00:24:37,680
When he gets well, we'll invite
Luffy to these chambers alone.

406
00:24:38,280 --> 00:24:40,020
Show some self-restraint.

407
00:24:40,220 --> 00:24:41,280
What nonsense.

408
00:24:41,660 --> 00:24:42,740
I am an empress.

409
00:24:42,860 --> 00:24:44,217
You can't tell me what to do.

410
00:24:44,300 --> 00:24:45,160
No means no.

411
00:24:45,560 --> 00:24:48,897
The well-being of this country
does not revolve around you.

412
00:24:48,980 --> 00:24:50,360
You poor girl.

413
00:24:50,620 --> 00:24:53,517
You've been stricken by the
most vile illness imaginable.

414
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:58,020
To think that our fearsome pirate
empress is lovesick of all things?

415
00:24:58,660 --> 00:25:00,857
Luffy must have gone
through hell and back!

416
00:25:00,940 --> 00:25:02,837
Surviving both Impel Down!

417
00:25:02,920 --> 00:25:05,977
And the terrible things that
happened at Navy headquarters!

418
00:25:06,060 --> 00:25:07,857
Despite my protest!

419
00:25:07,940 --> 00:25:12,477
The fact that he made it back here
alive is nothing short of a miracle.

420
00:25:12,560 --> 00:25:16,300
I can't help but wonder
what the gods expect of him?

421
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:19,597
Yo, pass me the wrench!

422
00:25:19,680 --> 00:25:20,800
Okay, here you go.

423
00:25:21,580 --> 00:25:24,160
Hey, how are the ship
repairs coming along?

424
00:25:24,440 --> 00:25:26,177
We'll manage, don't you worry.

425
00:25:26,260 --> 00:25:28,537
The rest of you ever figure
out where Straw Hat went?

426
00:25:28,620 --> 00:25:30,717
Team Bay's been gone for a while now, too.

427
00:25:30,800 --> 00:25:32,160
Nope, ain't got a clue.

428
00:25:34,020 --> 00:25:36,717
Someone told me that if
a man enters Amazon Lily,

429
00:25:36,800 --> 00:25:39,097
he'll be turned to
stone right on the spot.

430
00:25:39,180 --> 00:25:41,697
I'm starting to think it's
worth dying for, though.

431
00:25:41,780 --> 00:25:43,133
According to Afalandra,

432
00:25:43,280 --> 00:25:46,986
there are tons of girls, way more
than what we saw at the port.

433
00:25:47,220 --> 00:25:48,617
This is a one-time chance.

434
00:25:48,700 --> 00:25:52,077
If I don't peek, I might regret
it for the rest of my life.

435
00:25:52,160 --> 00:25:54,197
I guess we'll both be statues then, huh?

436
00:25:54,280 --> 00:25:56,117
Do you think they've got girl bears?

437
00:25:56,200 --> 00:25:57,788
You're ruining our fantasy!

438
00:25:58,120 --> 00:25:59,280
Sorry I asked.

439
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:00,980
Amazon women are humans!

440
00:26:01,240 --> 00:26:02,360
No bears for you!

441
00:26:02,520 --> 00:26:03,520
Life is cruel.

442
00:26:39,980 --> 00:26:41,560
What is this place?

443
00:26:41,840 --> 00:26:42,840
Where am I?

444
00:26:45,280 --> 00:26:47,800
Maybe I dreamt the whole thing.

445
00:27:03,500 --> 00:27:04,837
Sorry, Luffy.

446
00:27:04,920 --> 00:27:06,240
I tried.

447
00:27:10,220 --> 00:27:14,160
But looks like this is as far as I can go.

448
00:27:23,420 --> 00:27:25,200
It's not true!

449
00:27:25,520 --> 00:27:26,600
It can't be!

450
00:27:27,400 --> 00:27:28,230
Loopy!

451
00:27:29,600 --> 00:27:31,340
Go away!

452
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:40,360
Stop it!

453
00:27:40,520 --> 00:27:41,700
It's not true!

454
00:28:00,700 --> 00:28:03,200
Oh, my God.

455
00:28:21,820 --> 00:28:24,938
Jinbei, I know I might not
make it out of this alive.

456
00:28:25,520 --> 00:28:29,600
I'm sorry, but if I die, would
you look after my brother for me?

457
00:28:32,260 --> 00:28:34,220
You must listen to me, Luffy.

458
00:28:35,100 --> 00:28:37,420
Your brother Ace is... Don't say it!

459
00:28:37,680 --> 00:28:38,798
Don't say anything!

460
00:28:40,760 --> 00:28:42,520
You think I don't know?

461
00:28:43,180 --> 00:28:45,280
You think I think this is a dream?

462
00:28:47,040 --> 00:28:50,300
If it were a dream, I'd already be awake.

463
00:28:53,300 --> 00:28:55,820
But it's not, is it?

464
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:07,480
My brother Ace is really dead, isn't he?

465
00:29:15,260 --> 00:29:17,460
Yes, I'm afraid that he is.

466
00:29:26,060 --> 00:29:29,060
Hey, Grandpa, who's this Ace Fall?

467
00:29:29,600 --> 00:29:31,440
Well, funny you should ask.

468
00:29:32,820 --> 00:29:35,644
Because Ace is going to
be your new big brother.

469
00:29:38,100 --> 00:29:41,380
Luffy, when next we meet,
we'll both be top pirates.

470
00:29:42,960 --> 00:29:44,960
The top, you and me.

471
00:30:00,620 --> 00:30:02,020
Ace!
